1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,760
How to manage updates for standard deployments of BIRT Suite Enterprise Edition.

2
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:12,240
Please note in order to perform an update, Enterprise Server needs network access to

3
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:17,120
portswigger.net. Additionally, updates work differently for Kubernetes deployments.

4
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:21,800
For more information on updating Kubernetes deployments, please see our documentation

5
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:27,240
updating BIRT Suite Enterprise Edition on Kubernetes. Now as a first step, we can

6
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:33,540
configure automatic updates if we navigate to settings and updates. We'll see here that

7
00:00:33,540 --> 00:00:40,000
we have automatic updates enabled for both the Enterprise Server and BIRT scanner.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:46,560
We can disable one or both. If we would prefer to manually check for updates, we

9
00:00:46,560 --> 00:00:50,400
can select the check for updates button at any time and the system will let us know

10
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:55,380
which updates are available and we can select the install update button to have

11
00:00:55,380 --> 00:01:00,600
that update installed. If your Enterprise Server does not have network access, you can

12
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:04,980
also manually update both BIRT scanner and BIRT Suite Enterprise Edition and this

13
00:01:04,980 --> 00:01:09,420
ensures that you benefit from the latest improvements in scan checks. To do so,

14
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:16,080
navigate to our release page, select Enterprise and the relevant release. Now

15
00:01:16,080 --> 00:01:19,280
from the drop-down you can select updater and this will apply to the Enterprise

16
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:25,940
server update itself or BIRT scanner if you want to update BIRT scanner. Once the file has

17
00:01:25,940 --> 00:01:32,440
been downloaded, we can navigate back to Enterprise and select upload zip file. Please

18
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:35,720
note that BIRT Suite Enterprise Edition sends out automated email notifications

19
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:40,440
whenever a new update is available. In order to receive these updates, you will need to

20
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:44,360
connect BIRT Suite Enterprise Edition to your email server. For more information on this,

21
00:01:44,360 --> 00:01:50,780
please see our documentation configuring your SMTP server. Also note that there may be some downtime

22
00:01:50,780 --> 00:01:56,480
during updates and the impact of applying an update in terms of downtime is as follows. Updates

23
00:01:56,480 --> 00:02:01,180
to BIRT Suite Enterprise Edition will cause some downtime while the update is applied. The web UI,

24
00:02:01,180 --> 00:02:07,640
REST API and GraphQL API will be unavailable during the update and any scans that are configured to

25
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:12,640
start during the update will be delayed until it is completed. Scans that are already running at the

26
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:17,980
time of the update are unaffected. To reduce the impact of downtime, you can restrict automatic

27
00:02:17,980 --> 00:02:23,320
updates of BIRT Suite Enterprise Edition to specific date and times. Updates to BIRT

28
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:27,700
Scanner do not cause any downtime. Scans that are already running at the time of the update will

29
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:33,500
continue using the version of BIRT Scanner that they started with. New scans that start after the

30
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:38,560
update will use the updated version of BIRT Scanner. We do recommend that you enable automatic

31
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:45,160
updates of BIRT Scanner to make sure that the latest scan checks are available. Over time,

32
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:50,260
there might be backwards compatibility limitations on either component in relation to the other. If

33
00:02:50,260 --> 00:02:54,940
one component has not been updated for some time, you may have to update it before any further updates

34
00:02:54,940 --> 00:03:00,020
can be made to the other component. As you can see here, the updates page will indicate if this is the

35
00:03:00,020 --> 00:03:05,240
case. Some updates might also require manual intervention. For example, you may have to

36
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:10,200
accept changes to the software license agreement before an update can be applied. Again, the updates

37
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:13,360
page will indicate this if that's the case. Thank you.

